# Slidesmith is bring-your-own-keys. The easiest way to configure it is the
# in-app Settings screen — keys are saved to ~/.slidesmith/config.json.
#
# These env vars are optional overrides for self-hosting / headless setups:

# Port the local Slidesmith server listens on (default 8787).
# PORT=8787

# Interface to bind (default 127.0.0.1 — loopback only). DO NOT expose it to a
# network unless you're behind a firewall (or have set APP_PASSWORD below)
# and know what you're doing.
# HOST=127.0.0.1

# Where config + the generation queue are stored (default ~/.slidesmith).
# SLIDESMITH_DIR=/path/to/data

# You do NOT need to put API keys here — enter them in Settings instead.
# (post-bridge key for scheduling/posting/analytics, OpenRouter key for the AI.)

# ── Shared deployments (Vercel) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only relevant if you're deploying Slidesmith somewhere public so more than
# one person can use it — see "Deploying for a team (Vercel)" in the README.
# Not needed for local self-hosting.

# Requires anyone using the deployment to enter this password once before the
# app (and therefore your API keys) is reachable at all. Strongly recommended
# for any public deployment.
# APP_PASSWORD=choose-a-shared-password

# Set automatically by Vercel once you attach a Blob store from the project's
# Storage tab (Create Database → Blob) — you shouldn't need to set this by hand.
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN
